            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="0990" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8632</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-24T00:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1918, midnight</hi></date>. <lb/>
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 25, 3.16 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8390. Your 6310, January 21, 7 p.m. A full report on British action touching
                    Persia will be given to me by Mr. Balfour
                    in a few days prepared with reference to your inquiry. British wish and effort
                    is to uphold Persian independence and any help we may give will be appreciated.
                    Before report is ready the only practical suggestion thrown out was sending
                    American officers to stiffen up Persian Army. They … can be greatly helped by
                    good military leaders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
